/target
/build
# Local asset library mirrored from PolyHaven (and similar). Categorized
# scratch space; copy into godot/assets/ when an asset is actually used.
# See scripts/fetch_polyhaven_textures.py.
/asset-library/
# Scratch space for raw downloads + foliage cropping work — nothing here
# is canonical. `foliage_billboards/` carries the Megascans Billboard
# atlases for offline cropping into per-species `<species>_card.png`
# (see GroundFoliageScatterer SPECIES → `card` field).
/asset_downloads/
# Asset directories are opt-in: the parent is ignored, subdirectories
# are negated one-by-one as they become canonical to the project. Bulk
# binary content (HDRIs, textures, heightmaps) is routed through Git
# LFS via .gitattributes; UI-layer vector assets live in regular git.
/godot/assets/*
!/godot/assets/NOTICE.md
!/godot/assets/fonts/
!/godot/assets/icons/
!/godot/assets/logos/
!/godot/assets/backdrops/
!/godot/assets/environments/
!/godot/assets/terrain/
# Procedural placement caches — gitignored. Bakes are derived from
# `seed + cache_version` and the scatter scripts, so they're cheap to
# regenerate locally (Bake whole map / Bake near origin) and don't
# need to live in git. When a map's bake is final and we want every
# checkout to share an identical world, opt that map in here:
#   !/godot/assets/foliage_bake/<map_id>/
#   !/godot/assets/foliage_bake/<map_id>/**
godot/bin/
node_modules/
*.log
.env
*.pcap
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/state/*
!.claude/state/.gitignore
.claude/settings.local.json
# MCP server config: paths point at the dev's own home dir (Node entry,
# blender-mcp binary), so it can't be the same across contributors.
# The committed `godot/addons/godot_mcp/` works without it; the JSON is
# only consumed by the local Claude Code setup.
.mcp.json

# Godot
godot/.godot/
godot/.noosphere/

# SIMN engine is vendored read-only from the public SIMN repo by
# scripts/sync-simn.sh — not committed here. The pin lives in
# scripts/SIMN_VERSION; run the script before building. Only the synced
# addon is ignored; the other addons under godot/addons/ stay committed.
/godot/addons/simn/
# Per-session resources (character saves, clouds authoring, etc) are
# not versioned; the canonical UI theme + materials live in git.
godot/resources/*
!godot/resources/theme/
!godot/resources/materials/
!godot/resources/terrain/
!godot/resources/terrain/**
!godot/resources/foliage/
!godot/resources/foliage/**
!godot/resources/default_environment.tres
# `.import` files are normally noise — but Godot needs them to
# remember import settings for committed assets. Allowlist per
# directory the engine actually pulls from.
*.import
!godot/resources/**/*.import
!godot/assets/textures/terrain/**/*.import
*.uid

# Terrain texture pack: parent ignored by /godot/assets/* above, but
# the specific bundles the terrain shader references are allowlisted
# here so everyone picks up the same 4K diffuse + companions via LFS.
# Extend this list (alongside the TERRAIN_CLASS_DIFFUSE* arrays in
# crates/simn-godot/src/terrain.rs) when adding new shader variants.
!/godot/assets/models/
godot/assets/models/*
!godot/assets/models/plants/
!godot/assets/models/plants/**/
!godot/assets/models/plants_1k/
!godot/assets/models/plants_1k/**/
!godot/assets/models/plants_fab/
!godot/assets/models/plants_fab/**/
!godot/assets/models/plants_cgtrader/
!godot/assets/models/plants_cgtrader/**/
!godot/assets/models/trees/
!godot/assets/models/trees/**/
!godot/assets/models/forest_debris/
!godot/assets/models/forest_debris/**/
!godot/assets/models/trash/
!godot/assets/models/trash/**/
!/godot/assets/textures/
godot/assets/textures/*
!godot/assets/textures/terrain/
godot/assets/textures/terrain/*
!godot/assets/textures/terrain/megascans/
!godot/assets/textures/terrain/megascans/**/
!godot/assets/textures/terrain/aerial_grass_rock_4k.gltf/
!godot/assets/textures/terrain/aerial_ground_rock_4k.gltf/
